-- title:
--   H AConsistency Error Le Nu Of Pos
-- statement:
--   **The line-consistency error plus the transport term fits inside the induction scale.**
--
--   Let `params` be LDT parameters, let $\varepsilon,\delta,\gamma,\zeta\ge0$, and let $k\in\mathbb{N}$ satisfy $1\le k$. Define
--
--   $$
--   B=44k^2m\left(\varepsilon^{1/32}+\delta^{1/32}+\gamma^{1/32}+\zeta^{1/32}+\left(\frac{d}{q}\right)^{1/32}\right).
--   $$
--
--   Then the exact comparison is
--
--   $$
--   B+\sqrt{8m\min(\varepsilon,1)+4\min(\delta,1)}\le100k^2m\left(\varepsilon^{1/32}+\delta^{1/32}+\gamma^{1/32}+\zeta^{1/32}+\left(\frac{d}{q}\right)^{1/32}\right).
--   $$
--
--   The first term is `hBConsistencyError` and the right side is `ldPastingInInductionNu`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.hAConsistency_error_le_nu_of_pos`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
